  "script": "Your Claude bill is mostly the reading, not the writing — here's why the top fix barely helps.\nAnthropic's docs: the model remembers nothing between messages — every turn re-sends the whole conversation at input rates.\nBack to that popular fix.\nCaveman makes Claude answer in fewer words.\nA hundred thousand stars, and it does cut output.\nBut its README admits: input is untouched, and it adds over a thousand input tokens a turn.\nSo it trims the cheap half of your bill — that's why it barely helps.\nThese three cut the expensive half.\nOne: see it — ccusage charts each session's cost; claude-hud is a live meter in your status line.\nTwo: Ponytail stops Claude rebuilding code that already exists — it checks the standard library first.\nThree: between unrelated tasks, type slash-clear — free. Compact re-reads everything to summarise it.\nThey run with your agent's permissions — read them first.\nComment CLAUDE, I'll send all four.",
